// t_5c12df56 positive twin of fp_return_half_depth_control_f.cg: here the
// HALF is the colour and the out parameter is something else.
//
// No out parameter binds COLOR0, so the return type decides: the colour is
// H0 at fp16 with outputFromH0 set, while the fp32 DEPTH out parameter is
// untouched.  The reference emits colour word 0x1E800140 and depth word
// 0x08030100; ours matches both once the return type is read.
//
// The pair matters because the two fixtures differ only in WHICH output is
// half: a rule that looked at the return type alone would set the flag on
// both, and a rule that looked at parameters alone would set it on
// neither.
half4 main(out float d : DEPTH) : COLOR
{
    d = 0.5;
    return 1.0;
}
